{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. Clear sensing drives forward-biased exploration, while any obstacle forces a dedicated recovery state first. Front obstacles trigger a rare one-shot backward escape before a directed turn; side obstacles trigger a one-shot turn away from the blocked side. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, but safety-critical obstacle events can redirect recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with two plant automata",
    "Use one policy specification with perception states and one-shot action states",
    "Bias clear operation to move_forward, with random_walk only as a secondary clear-mode option",
    "Force obstacle_front through brief move_backward recovery, then directed turning",
    "Force obstacle_left to rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right to rotate_counterclockwise",
    "Return to forward exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery"
  ],
